From 3d6074d1eae8fb54d02f6e67df4f49420a723067 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:53:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] drm/gma500: run dummy transfers on the SGX545 transfer
 queue

Add builders for the firmware's transfer command and HW transfer context
(sgx_xfer.c, pinned by KUnit) and a test area in the kernel data heap: a
64 KiB client CCB, its control block, a context and two scratch words.
dri/N/sgx/xfer_dummy queues one DUMMYTRANSFER and checks each effect: the
memory update and status write, the client CCB read offset, the context
count, and one SW_EVENT interrupt. This exercises the firmware's whole
transfer path except the render, and the interrupt path.

On the GMA3600 every effect shows up about 140 us after the kick, for each of
eleven transfers in a row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
